    "result": "Perfect! The bug is now fixed. Here's a summary of what was wrong and how I fixed it:\n\n## Problem\nThe `frai gate init --ci` command was creating `FRAI-SPEC.md` but not `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`. The `--ci` flag wasn't being passed to the underlying `frai-gate` CLI.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe main `frai` program defines `--ci` as a top-level option. When you run `frai gate init --ci`, Commander.js was parsing `--ci` as an option for the main program, not passing it as part of the arguments to the `gate` subcommand.\n\n## Solution\nI updated the `gate` command's action handler in `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` to:\n\n1. Accept the `command` parameter (the third parameter in Commander.js action handlers)\n2. Extract the parent command's options using `command.parent?.opts?.()`\n3. Check if `parentOptions.ci` is set and manually add `--ci` to the arguments passed to `frai-gate`\n4. Also handle any other flags from the subcommand's own options\n\n## Verification\n\u2705 After rebuilding with `pnpm --filter frai build`, running `node packages/frai-cli/dist/index.js gate init --ci` now correctly creates both files:\n- `FRAI-SPEC.md` \u2713\n- `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` \u2713",
